    "France and Spain lead the field as the top two sides in the latest FIFA rankings, buoyed by consistent results in Nations League and European qualifiers alongside deep squads featuring elite attacking talent. England sits just behind on the strength of its midfield control and recent form, while Argentina and Brazil retain strong positioning thanks to Copa America pedigree and individual star power. The expanded 48-team format and balanced group-stage matchups further compress probabilities, as several other nations post solid recent results and favorable paths. This tight clustering mirrors the depth across the top tier entering the June kickoff."
